From 61962a359292d116c149861a394245594807fd43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nanairo8890 <301115931+nanairo8890@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:37:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] input: goodix: report fingerprint presses and take touch
 modes from xiaomi_touch

The stock fingerprint and touch feature components of mondrian set touch
modes through /dev/xiaomi-touch and wait on fod_press_status. The Goodix
Berlin driver had its own gesture nodes only, so neither worked. Connect
it to xiaomi_touch the way Xiaomi's GT9916 driver (marble-s-oss
goodix_9916) does, in a separate file:

- Touch_Doubletap_Mode, Touch_Fod_Enable and Touch_Aod_Enable or
  Touch_FodIcon_Enable set the double tap, FOD and single tap bits of the
  gesture mask; the other modes are stored and reported as unsupported
  (0..0) values
- A mode change while the touch is asleep is applied at once: the touch
  is woken and suspended again with the new mask, under the PM lock and
  from a freezable work item
- fod_press_status follows the FOD-DOWN and FOD-UP gestures with the
  screen off and the fingerprint flag of the touch events with the screen
  on; it is cleared at resume and when FOD-UP arrives with FOD disabled
- Single tap notifies gesture_single_tap_state and the suspend state
  follows the touch

Builds without xiaomi_touch too: the glue is compiled out when it is not
reachable. goodix_core now depends on xiaomi_touch, as the stock module.
Xiaomi's interface has no unregister call, so the touch module must not
be unloaded while xiaomi_touch stays loaded
